  "body": "Adds the yellow `needs-maintainer` review label to the process docs. It's already created on GitHub and applied to #359 and #364.\n\n**Why:** a review that ends \"Not built - needs a maintainer look\" had no label to set. That verdict covers a new dependency, or a `build.rs` / scripts / `.github` change the reviewer reads but doesn't build. Without a label, such a PR looked unreviewed on the PR list.\n\n**What changed:**\n- `.claude/skills/review-prs/SKILL.md` step 2b: a fourth row in the label table, the rule (no blockers -> `needs-maintainer`; blockers -> `needs-rework` as before), and how the owner clears it.\n- `.claude/agents/PR-reviewer.md`: the verdict line names the label.\n- `README.md` review-labels table and `AGENTS.md` review-label sentence: the new row and the new clause.\n\nDocs and process only: no code, no tests.\n\nChangelog: none\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
